# ES-4 is the SINGLE-NODE variant: one api-es container owning host :8080.
# Auto-loaded by docker compose for EVERY command, so the value stays sticky.
#
# REPLICAS drives API_REPLICAS, which sets the saga per-node claim =
# ceil(total-segments / replicas). It MUST equal the number of API containers actually
# running, or segments are left unclaimed (too low) / over-subscribed (too high).
#
# Raising it here alone does NOT scale the stack — this branch has no nginx service and
# api-es publishes :8080 directly, so a second replica would fail to bind. The multi-replica
# topology (nginx load balancer, deploy.replicas, max_connections=1000) lives on
# ES-3-pesimistic-scaling; monitoring/nginx/nginx.conf is kept here so it is one edit away.
REPLICAS=1
